  "id": "floristgump",
  "neon": "#ff7ab8",
  "note": "FLORIST GUMP — the florist on Meltwater Row, across the road from the park and its statue.\n\nThe tile's prose: flowers on the pavement in galvanised buckets, three deep, pulled in at dusk; a\nwindow that is mostly wreath frames; the sign painted in a loopy hand.\n\nSo the pavement is the shop: three rows of buckets across the front, each a different colour, under\na striped canopy. The window behind them is lit green with the frames in it, the door is at one\nend, and the name is painted in script on the fascia. The flat upstairs has two sash windows. The\nrender is cream, which is what makes the flowers the brightest thing on the row.",
  "pal": "ty_stuff",
